  "goodToKnow": "Der Gleichstrom is direct current (DC), as supplied by batteries and solar panels. The opposite is der Wechselstrom (AC), used in household sockets. Germany is building long HVDC lines (Hochspannungs-Gleichstrom-Übertragung), such as SuedLink, to carry wind power from the north to the industrial south. Der Strom means current or electricity, and also a big river."
